For those who -- like me -- missed these days and never played the
very first Nethack version released, now you can:

After discussing whether Nethack or Perl was older on our local LUG
(Linux User Goup) -- don't ask why this question might be of any
importance, it really isn't -- and some researching (Nethack is in
fact older by about five months) we dug up the original sources from
an usenet archive.

Unfortunately the old sources can't be build on a modern system out of
the box, so I hacked them a bit up -- and now they compile and run on
a nowadays GNU/Linux system.  :-)

So for all of you interested in time traveling, here is the tarball
with the modified sources:

http://www.sha-bang.de/content/18_nethack/nethack-1.3d-revived_20071013.tar.gz

The current revived sources can always be found on my homepage
(german, just look out for the dowload link):

http://www.sha-bang.de/index.php?page=18_nethack

A README.revived with further details can be found in the archive and
online in the SCM:

http://hg.intevation.de/nethack/history/nethack-1.3d-revived/raw-file/tip/README.revived

Apropos SCM, those who are interested in the detailed changes (and
maybe in contributing) the mercurial[0] repository with all changes
can be found online at:

http://hg.intevation.de/nethack/history/nethack-1.3d-revived

cheers
